From d5e4ee577e1dd6c0e6140411b587c669210d10b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "5455945@gmail.com" <5455945@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 16:26:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] tools: add Gaia-compatible afree login service

Add a dependency-free Node.js service that implements the sign-in
protocol Chromium speaks, so an unmodified client can sign in to it by
passing --gaia-config.

Protocol details are taken from the Chromium tree:
  * DICE sign-in is signalled with X-Chrome-ID-Consistency-Response
    (components/signin/core/browser/dice_header_helper.cc).
  * /ListAccounts is a cookie-authenticated POST returning
    base64(binary gaia.ListAccountsResponse)
    (google_apis/gaia/list_accounts_response.proto).
  * /oauth2/v4/token handles authorization_code and refresh_token
    grants (google_apis/gaia/gaia_auth_fetcher.cc).
  * /oauth/multilogin accepts MultiBearer and returns XSSI-prefixed
    JSON cookies (google_apis/gaia/oauth_multilogin_result.cc).
  * GaiaCookieManagerService watches SAPISID on google_url/secure_google_url,
    so the generated config overrides those origins too.

Contents:
  * SQLite (node:sqlite) schema for users, sessions, session_accounts,
    auth codes, refresh/access tokens and audit log.
  * scrypt password hashing, hashed single-use tokens, login throttle.
  * Admin CLI for users, sessions and gaia-config generation.
  * 15 end-to-end protocol tests.
