+# afree login service
+
+A small, dependency-free Node.js service that speaks the **same sign-in
+protocol as Google Gaia**, so an unmodified (or barely modified) Chromium /
+afree client can sign in to it by pointing `--gaia-config` at it.
+
+- Sign in with your own accounts when the service is configured.
+- Sign in with Google normally when it is not.
+- The client-side protocol is the real one: DICE response headers, binary
+  protobuf for `ListAccounts`, OAuth2 token exchange, MultiBearer
+  `/oauth/multilogin` cookies.
+
+```
+Chromium / afree                         this service                 SQLite
+  │                                          │                          │
+  │ GET /signin/chrome/sync?ssp=1&continue=  │                          │
+  │─────────────────────────────────────────>│  login form (HTML)       │
+  │ POST email+password (same URL)           │                          │
+  │─────────────────────────────────────────>│  verify (scrypt) ───────>│
+  │ 200 + Set-Cookie: SID/LSID/HSID/...      │                          │
+  │     + X-Chrome-ID-Consistency-Response   │  create auth code ──────>│
+  │<─────────────────────────────────────────│                          │
+  │ POST /oauth2/v4/token (authorization_code)│                         │
+  │─────────────────────────────────────────>│  issue tokens ──────────>│
+  │ POST /ListAccounts (cookies)             │  base64 binary proto     │
+  │─────────────────────────────────────────>│                          │
+  │ POST /oauth/multilogin (MultiBearer)     │  )]}' JSON cookies       │
+  │─────────────────────────────────────────>│                          │
+```
+
+## What Chromium actually expects
+
+These are the details that make a "highly compatible" server, all taken from
+the Chromium tree:
+
+| Behaviour | Source of truth |
+| --- | --- |
+| Sign-in URL is `<gaia_url>/signin/chrome/sync?ssp=1` | `google_apis/gaia/gaia_urls.cc` |
+| Login result is a **HTTP response header**, `X-Chrome-ID-Consistency-Response: action=SIGNIN,authuser=0,id=…,email=…,authorization_code=…` | `components/signin/core/browser/dice_header_helper.cc` |
+| That header is only processed for responses on the Gaia origin | `chrome/browser/signin/chrome_signin_helper.cc` |
+| `/ListAccounts` is a **POST with cookies** and returns **base64 of a binary `gaia.ListAccountsResponse`** | `google_apis/gaia/gaia_auth_fetcher.cc`, `google_apis/gaia/gaia_auth_util.cc` |
+| `Account` fields: `display_email=3`, `valid_session=9`, `obfuscated_id=10`, `signed_out=14`, `is_verified=15` | `google_apis/gaia/list_accounts_response.proto` |
+| The cookie listener watches **SAPISID** and `google_url`'s host | `google_apis/gaia/gaia_constants.h`, `components/signin/internal/identity_manager/gaia_cookie_manager_service.cc` |
+| The auth code is exchanged at `<google_apis_origin_url>/oauth2/v4/token` with `grant_type=authorization_code`, `scope`, `client_id`, `client_secret`, `code` | `google_apis/gaia/gaia_auth_fetcher.cc` |
+| `/oauth/multilogin` receives `Authorization: MultiBearer <token>:<gaia_id>,…` and answers `)]}'\n{"status":"OK","cookies":[…]}` | `google_apis/gaia/gaia_auth_fetcher.cc`, `google_apis/gaia/oauth_multilogin_result.cc` |
+| DICE is **disabled** unless an OAuth client id + secret are configured | `chrome/browser/signin/account_consistency_mode_manager.cc` |
+
+That last row is the one that trips people up: a Chromium build with
+`google_api_key=false` cannot sign in at all until an OAuth client is
+configured, because `HasOAuthClientConfigured()` returns false. The generated
+`gaia-config.json` fixes this by setting the API-key entries as well.
+
+## Requirements
+
+- Node.js **>= 22.5** (uses the built-in `node:sqlite` module).
+  This Chromium checkout already ships one:
+  `third_party/node/linux/node-linux-x64/bin/node` (v24, SQLite 3.50).
+- No npm packages, no codegen, no build step.
+
+## Quick start
+
+```sh
+cd tools/afree-login-service
+
+# 1. create an account (reads the password from stdin)
+printf '%s\n' 'your-password' |
+  node src/cli.mjs add-user --email you@example.com --name "You"
+
+# 2. start the service
+node src/server.mjs --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8080
+
+# 3. generate the Chromium config
+node src/cli.mjs gen-gaia-config --url http://127.0.0.1:8080 \
+  > gaia-config.json
+```
+
+Then start the client with the generated config:
+
+```sh
+# Linux
+out/<your-out-dir>/afree \
+  --gaia-config="$PWD/gaia-config.json" \
+  --user-data-dir=/tmp/afree-profile
+
+# Windows (cmd.exe)
+out\winx64r\afree.exe ^
+  --gaia-config=C:\path\to\gaia-config.json ^
+  --user-data-dir=%TEMP%\afree-profile
+```
+
+Open `afree://settings/people`, click **Sign in**, and use the account you
+created. To go back to Google, just drop `--gaia-config`.
+
+If you prefer explicit switches instead of `--gaia-config`:
+
+```sh
+--gaia-url=http://127.0.0.1:8080
+--google-apis-url=http://127.0.0.1:8080
+--lso-url=http://127.0.0.1:8080
+--google-url=http://127.0.0.1:8080
+--oauth2-client-id=afree-client-id
+--oauth2-client-secret=afree-client-secret
+```
+
+But note: `--oauth2-client-id/secret` only fill in `CLIENT_MAIN`; the other
+OAuth clients keep the `dummytoken` sentinel, `HasOAuthClientConfigured()`
+stays false and DICE stays disabled. Prefer `--gaia-config` with the
+`api_keys` block (or set `GOOGLE_DEFAULT_CLIENT_ID` /
+`GOOGLE_DEFAULT_CLIENT_SECRET`).
+
+### HTTPS (recommended for anything but localhost)
+
+Chromium treats `http://127.0.0.1` and `http://localhost` as trustworthy, so
+plain HTTP is fine for local tests. For a real deployment, terminate TLS in
+front of the service and start it with an https origin so `Secure` cookies are
+emitted:
+
+```sh
+node src/server.mjs \
+  --public-url https://login.example.com \
+  --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8080
+```
+
+Then point Chromium at `https://login.example.com`. With a self-signed
+certificate, add `--ignore-certificate-errors` for testing.
+
+## Endpoints
+
+| Method | Path | Purpose |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| GET | `/signin/chrome/sync` | Sign-in form (`ssp=1`, `continue=`, `flow=`, `email_hint=`) |
+| POST | `/signin/chrome/sync` | Authenticate, set cookies, return the DICE header |
+| GET/POST | `/ServiceLogin`, `/ServiceLoginAuth`, `/AccountChooser`, `/AddSession`, `/embedded/...` | Legacy / edge sign-in entry points |
+| GET/POST | `/ListAccounts` | base64 binary `gaia.ListAccountsResponse` |
+| POST | `/oauth2/v4/token` | `authorization_code` and `refresh_token` grants |
+| GET/POST | `/oauth2/v1/userinfo` | Profile for a Bearer access token |
+| GET/POST | `/oauth2/v2/tokeninfo` | Token introspection |
+| POST | `/oauth/multilogin` | Cookie propagation (`)]}'` prefixed JSON) |
+| GET | `/GetCheckConnectionInfo` | `[]` |
+| GET/POST | `/enable_sync` | `action=ENABLE_SYNC` DICE header |
+| GET/POST | `/Logout` | Clear cookies + `Google-Accounts-SignOut` header |
+| POST | `/o/oauth2/revoke` | Revoke a refresh token |
+| POST | `/RotateBoundCookies` | `400`, DBSC is not implemented |
+| POST | `/reauth/v1beta/users/...` | `400`, reauth is not implemented |
+| GET | `/` | Status page with the endpoint list |
+| GET | `/healthz` | `{"status":"ok"}` |
+
+## Generated `gaia-config.json`
+
+`gen-gaia-config` produces the URL overrides **and** the API-key overrides:
+
+```json
+{
+  "urls": {
+    "google_url":            {"url": "http://127.0.0.1:8080"},
+    "secure_google_url":     {"url": "http://127.0.0.1:8080"},
+    "gaia_url":              {"url": "http://127.0.0.1:8080"},
+    "lso_origin_url":        {"url": "http://127.0.0.1:8080"},
+    "google_apis_origin_url":{"url": "http://127.0.0.1:8080"},
+    "oauth_account_manager_origin_url": {"url": "http://127.0.0.1:8080"},
+    "oauth_account_manager_mtls_origin_url": {"url": "http://127.0.0.1:8080"},
+    "oauth2_mtls_origin_url": {"url": "http://127.0.0.1:8080"},
+    "account_capabilities_origin_url": {"url": "http://127.0.0.1:8080"},
+    "people_api_origin_url":  {"url": "http://127.0.0.1:8080"},
+    "classroom_api_origin_url": {"url": "http://127.0.0.1:8080"},
+    "tasks_api_origin_url":   {"url": "http://127.0.0.1:8080"}
+  },
+  "api_keys": {
+    "GOOGLE_DEFAULT_CLIENT_ID":     "afree-client-id",
+    "GOOGLE_DEFAULT_CLIENT_SECRET": "afree-client-secret",
+    "GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID_MAIN":        "afree-client-id",
+    "GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET_MAIN":    "afree-client-secret"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+Why each key matters:
+
+- `gaia_url` — used for the sign-in URL, `/ListAccounts`, `/Logout`,
+  `/oauth/multilogin`, and as the origin that Chromium accepts the DICE header
+  from (`HasGaiaSchemeHostPort`).
+- `google_url` / `secure_google_url` — the cookie listener origin and the host
+  used to validate GAIA cookies. Must match the host that sets the cookies.
+- `google_apis_origin_url` — `/oauth2/v4/token`, `/oauth2/v1/userinfo`,
+  `/oauth2/v2/tokeninfo`.
+- `lso_origin_url` — `/o/oauth2/revoke`.
+- `api_keys` — enables DICE at all (see the warning above).
+
+## Accounts, sessions and tokens
+
+- Passwords are hashed with **scrypt** (N=16384, r=8, p=1, 64-byte key).
+- One **session** per browser sign-in, represented by the `SID` cookie. This is
+  the "multi-device" model: phone, laptop and desktop each create their own
+  session and refresh token.
+- `session_accounts` stores the accounts attached to a session, in order. The
+  first one is the primary account reported by `/ListAccounts`.
+- Authorization codes are single-use, 5 minutes by default and stored hashed.
+- Access tokens live 1 hour; refresh tokens are revocable and by default do not
+  expire (`--refresh-token-ttl-days N` adds an expiry).
+- `audit_log` records `login_success`, `login_failed`, `token_issued`,
+  `logout`, `user_created`.
+
+Cookie values other than `SID` are derived with HMAC-SHA256 from the session id
+and a persistent server secret, so the server can re-emit them on
+`/oauth/multilogin` without storing six extra columns.
+
+### Admin CLI
+
+```sh
+node src/cli.mjs add-user        --email a@b.c [--password -] [--name X]
+node src/cli.mjs list-users
+node src/cli.mjs set-password    --email a@b.c [--password -]
+node src/cli.mjs disable-user    --email a@b.c
+node src/cli.mjs enable-user     --email a@b.c
+node src/cli.mjs delete-user     --email a@b.c
+node src/cli.mjs list-sessions   --email a@b.c
+node src/cli.mjs revoke-sessions --email a@b.c
+node src/cli.mjs prune
+node src/cli.mjs gen-gaia-config [--url https://login.example.com] [--output f]
+```
+
+All commands accept `--db <path>`; the default is `data/afree-login.sqlite3`.
+
+## Service options
+
+```
+--host 127.0.0.1                # bind address
+--port 8080
+--db data/afree-login.sqlite3
+--public-url http://host:port   # origin Chromium uses
+--access-token-ttl 3600
+--refresh-token-ttl-days 0      # 0 = no expiry
+--auth-code-ttl 300
+--session-ttl-days 30
+--log-level info                # debug|info|warn|error|silent
+--allow-registration            # enables /signup
+--redirect-continue             # redirect to ?continue= like Google Gaia
+--allowed-continue-hosts a,b    # allowlist for ?continue=
+--no-oauth-code-cookie          # drop the legacy oauth_code cookie
+```
+
+Environment variables use the `AFREE_LOGIN_` prefix
+(`AFREE_LOGIN_PORT`, `AFREE_LOGIN_PUBLIC_URL`, `AFREE_LOGIN_DB`, ...).
+
+By default the service renders its own "signed in" page after a successful
+login instead of following Chromium's `?continue=https://www.google.com/`,
+which keeps an offline deployment from ending on a network error page. The
+sign-in itself completes through the DICE header either way. Pass
+`--redirect-continue` for Gaia-faithful behaviour.
+
+## Database
+
+SQLite (WAL) through `node:sqlite`; in this tree that is SQLite **3.50.4**.
+Tables: `users`, `sessions`, `session_accounts`, `auth_codes`,
+`refresh_tokens`, `access_tokens`, `audit_log`, `meta`.
+
+The schema is applied idempotently at startup (`src/schema.sql`). `STRICT`
+tables and `PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON` are enabled.
+
+## Tests
+
+```sh
+node --disable-warning=ExperimentalWarning --test test/*.test.mjs
+```
+
+15 protocol tests cover the DICE header, cookie issuance, binary
+`ListAccounts` encoding, token exchange, single-use codes, userinfo,
+MultiBearer multilogin, ENABLE_SYNC and logout.
+
+## Current limitations
+
+- **Sync (bookmarks, history, …) is not implemented.** Sign-in works and the
+  refresh token can be used later for a `--sync-url` backend. Without one,
+  `afree://sync-internals` shows the account but sync stays disabled.
+- **DBSC / `RotateBoundCookies`** is not implemented (returns `400`).
+  `eligible_for_token_binding` is deliberately omitted.
+- **Reauth** (`AccountChooser`, `/reauth/v1beta/...`) is a stub.
+- **Multi-account** is supported by `/ListAccounts` (all accounts in the
+  session, primary first), but `/oauth/multilogin` only re-emits the primary
+  account's cookies; secondary-account cookie families (`__Secure-1PSID`, …)
+  are not modelled.
+- **SAML / embedded setup** for ChromeOS is not implemented.
+- Single-process, in-memory login throttle. For multiple instances, move the
+  throttle to SQLite or a shared cache and terminate TLS in front of the
+  service.
+
+## Security notes
+
+This service authenticates **your own** accounts. Do not import Google
+passwords into it, and do not point a trusted browser profile at an untrusted
+instance.
+
+- Use HTTPS (or loopback) so cookies are set with `Secure`.
+- Keep `data/` out of version control; it contains password hashes, tokens and
+  the cookie-signing secret (`.gitignore` already covers it).
+- `--allowed-continue-hosts` restricts the post-login redirect allowlist; with
+  the default (empty) any http(s) URL is accepted when `--redirect-continue` is
+  enabled.
+- The login page is same-origin and uses `SameSite=Lax` cookies. There is no
+  CSRF token because the form posts to the same URL; if you embed the service
+  behind a multi-origin front end, add one.
+
+## Roadmap
+
+1. `--sync-url` compatible backend for bookmarks/preferences (protobuf
+   `SyncEntity`, `/command` endpoints).
+2. Multi-account cookie families and per-account sign-out.
+3. Device-bound sessions (`RotateBoundCookies`, DBSC).
+4. Password change / account chooser pages.
